  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\n\nAn upper trough deepening along the Pacific NW coast is closing\noff over northern California while a northern stream trough is\nmoving east across the Prairie Provinces. This trough is\nresponsible for clouds and scattered showers from north-central\nMontana into southern Sask. These showers are expected to stay in\nnorth of the International border today but a few sprinkles \ncannot be ruled out from Whitewater to Plentywood today. \nElsewhere, clouds will lift northeast allowing increasing sunshine\nand temperatures starting to recover a bit.\n\nThe closed low is expected to lift into Montana by this weekend\nwith amounts from 0.50\" to 1.25\" in mainly the eastern and central\nzones with lighter amounts in the west. Most of the rainfall is\nexpected to move in Friday night and last into Saturday morning.\nthunderstorms Friday night will produce locally heavy rainfall.\n\nA weak upper ridge is expected in the wake of the departing upper\nlow by Monday for drying conditions and another slight bump in\ntemperatures.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n- NBM pops were too dry initially for early this morning, so \n  blended with higher pops through today (Wednesday). Other NBM \n  elements looked good.\n\n- Confidence in rain chances this weekend are moderate. There is a\n  higher confidence in rainfall chances across the eastern zones\n  of the CWA. Less confidence moving further into western zones.\n\n- Confidence in amounts are increasing but remain inconsistent\n  over the central zones.",
